===README===
# Music files

Two placeholder tracks stand in for the full soundtrack while MusicGen
work runs in parallel. The reader fetches `manifest.json` from the client
and plays the listed files. No code change is needed to ship real tracks.

## Swap in real tracks

1. Put the finished audio files under `public/music/`.
2. Edit `manifest.json`: keep the shape the `parseManifest` function in
   `core/music.ts` accepts, point `src` at the new files, and bump
   `version`.
3. Keep `src` values as `/music/` paths or `https` URLs. Remote URLs need
   a `media-src` addition in `next.config.ts`.

Validate with `npm test`. The manifest test loads the committed file
through `parseManifest` and checks that every local `src` exists.

## License note

MusicGen weights are CC-BY-NC. The clips here are test output from those
weights, so this demo stays non-commercial. The same rule covers the full
soundtrack when it lands.
